* 5-stage ring DCO for SpiceBind.
* Higher trim disconnects binary-weighted load capacitors -> higher frequency.
* Python str.format() fills VDD, TEMP, MODELS, CUNIT, TRAN_STEP, TRAN_STOP.
* Doubled braces are ngspice expressions (see tests/test.cir).

.param VDD={VDD}
.param CUNIT={CUNIT}
.temp {TEMP}
.include {MODELS}

.subckt inv a y vdd
M1 y a vdd vdd pdco w=4u l=0.35u
M2 y a 0   0   ndco w=2u l=0.35u
.ends inv

.subckt nand2 a b y vdd
Mp1 y a vdd vdd pdco w=4u l=0.35u
Mp2 y b vdd vdd pdco w=4u l=0.35u
Mn1 mid a 0   0   ndco w=2u l=0.35u
Mn2 y   b mid 0   ndco w=2u l=0.35u
.ends nand2

Vdd vdd 0 {{VDD}}

Venable enable 0 0 external
Vtrim[0] trim[0] 0 0 external
Vtrim[1] trim[1] 0 0 external
Vtrim[2] trim[2] 0 0 external
Vtrim[3] trim[3] 0 0 external

* Invert trim: trim=1 opens the cap switch (less C, faster).
Xit0 trim[0] ntrim0 vdd inv
Xit1 trim[1] ntrim1 vdd inv
Xit2 trim[2] ntrim2 vdd inv
Xit3 trim[3] ntrim3 vdd inv

* Ring. enable=0 holds n0 high through the NAND and stops oscillation.
Xen enable n4 n0 vdd nand2
X1 n0 n1 vdd inv
X2 n1 n2 vdd inv
X3 n2 n3 vdd inv
X4 n3 n4 vdd inv

Cfix n1 0 {{CUNIT}}
C0 n1 m0 {{CUNIT}}
C1 n1 m1 {{CUNIT*2}}
C2 n1 m2 {{CUNIT*4}}
C3 n1 m3 {{CUNIT*8}}
Ms0 m0 ntrim0 0 0 ndco w=8u l=0.35u
Ms1 m1 ntrim1 0 0 ndco w=8u l=0.35u
Ms2 m2 ntrim2 0 0 ndco w=8u l=0.35u
Ms3 m3 ntrim3 0 0 ndco w=8u l=0.35u

Xb1 n2 oscb vdd inv
Xb2 oscb osc vdd inv

* Kick the ring out of metastability.
.ic v(n0)=0 v(n2)={{VDD}}

.option reltol=1e-3 noinit
.tran {TRAN_STEP} {TRAN_STOP} uic
.end
